    "raw_output": "package solution\n\nimport \"errors\"\n\n// ReconcileLedger reconciles a ledger opening balance with a list of transactions.\n// Each transaction is a slice of three integers: [id, kind, amount].\n// kind 1 represents a credit (positive), -1 represents a debit (negative).\n//\n// Returns:\n//   - The new total balance after reconciliation.\n//   - A boolean indicating whether the reconciliation was successful.\n//\n// Reconciliation is considered successful if:\n//   1. No duplicate transaction IDs are found.\n//   2. All transaction kinds are valid (1 for credit, -1 for debit).\n//   3. All transaction amounts are positive integers.\n//   4. The arithmetic holds: opening + sum(credits) - sum(debits) = new balance.\n//\n// If any validation fails, the function returns 0 and false.\nfunc ReconcileLedger(opening int64, entries [][3]int64) (int64, bool) {\n\tif len(entries) == 0 {\n\t\treturn opening, true\n\t}\n\n\t// Track seen IDs to detect duplicates\n\tseenIDs := make(map[int64]bool)\n\t// Track total credits and debits\n\ttotalCredits := int64(0)\n\ttotalDebits := int64(0)\n\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tid := entry[0]\n\t\tkind := entry[1]\n\t\tamount := entry[2]\n\n\t\t// Validate ID uniqueness\n\t\tif seenIDs[id] {\n\t\t\treturn 0, false\n\t\t}\n\t\tseenIDs[id] = true\n\n\t\t// Validate kind\n\t\tif kind != 1 && kind != -1 {\n\t\t\treturn 0, false\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Validate amount\n\t\tif amount <= 0 {\n\t\t\treturn 0, false\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Update totals based on kind\n\t\tif kind == 1 {\n\t\t\ttotalCredits += amount\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\ttotalDebits += amount\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\t// Calculate expected balance\n\texpectedBalance := opening + totalCredits - totalDebits\n\n\t// Verify arithmetic consistency\n\tif expectedBalance != opening+totalCredits-totalDebits {\n\t\treturn 0, false\n\t}\n\n\treturn expectedBalance, true\n}<|im_end|>",
